lls  director christopher nolan actually had  the crew built an entire  set that rotated for the actor the  reasoning for it  christopher just doesn't like using cgi  effects very much  the same concept was used in this  euphoria episode  everything is just spinning and you have  no sense of where the real world  is the dark knight didn't stop at the  pencil trick or car chase for practical  effects  the plane escape scene was also 100 real  they used a prop plane but still had the  stuntman drop down into it to capture  the moment where the cia plane is  destroyed  for the inside shots they used the  simulator hallway that was built for  inception  reduce reuse recycle right yes  the fire rises imagine being able to  make bread in literal seconds  like rey did here well what if we told  you  you can it just might not taste very  good  the recipe rey poured into that ball was  an actual real concoction that the  production team spent three months  perfecting  if you want to try it at home a quick  google search will give you plenty of  recipes  60 portions  like we mentioned earlier christopher  isn't a huge fan of cgi  so the inception scene where the paris  street explodes was shot using air  cannons instead  they set off each one individually and  used a special camera to capture it all  in slow motion  check out how cool the behind the scenes  footage is we did tests with people  sitting in front  and we showed them to leo and showed it  to ellen mad max is just an overall  wild film so we aren't surprised that  the guitar flamethrower we see here  was actually real not to mention it was  also a working guitar  the actor and musician iota who was  tasked with working it had to practice  for over a month on the moving platform  and had to be able to bungee jump  blindfolded there's also a flamethrower  used in a battle against max himself the  rock may be  the rock but he still had to get his  stuntman to jump in for the cgi-less  scene  his stunt double was atta